<title>INDIA: Bombay bullion market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Bombay bullion market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombay bullion market was closed on Wednesday for Ashadh Ekadashi religious holiday. Market will reopen for trading on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday gold 24 carat was down by five rupees at 4,450 rupees per 10 gramme and silver (.999) was down by 45 rupees at 6,275 rupees per kg following losses in the world market.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.64 gramme) were down by 100 rupees at 52,000 rupees per piece.</p>
<p>($1=35.70 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
</text>
